10 REM 10 PRINT -- COOL8 EDITION
20 REM AFTER THE C64 ONE-LINER:
30 REM 10 PRINT CHR$(205.5+RND(1)); : GOTO 10
40 REM
50 REM MODE 1: TEXT, 40 COLUMNS, SO A CELL IS 16 WIDE
60 REM BY 16 HIGH AND THE DIAGONALS ARE SQUARE.
70 REM
80 REM THE PALETTE IS THE COMMODORE 64'S OWN, COPIED
90 REM ENTRY FOR ENTRY IN ITS OWN INDEX ORDER, SO 6 IS
100 REM BLUE AND 14 IS LIGHT BLUE AS THEY ARE THERE.
110 REM ATTRIBUTE $6E = BACKGROUND 6, FOREGROUND 14.
120 MODE 1
130 FOR I=0 TO 15
140 POKE $FF1E,I:READ R,G:POKE $FF1F,R:POKE $FF1F,G
150 NEXT
160 DATA 0,0,15,255,8,0,10,254
170 DATA 12,76,0,197,0,10,14,231
180 DATA 13,133,6,64,15,119,3,51
190 DATA 7,119,10,246,0,143,11,187
200 POKE $FF1A,14
210 B=PEEK($FF12)+PEEK($FF13)*256
220 S=PEEK($FF14)+PEEK($FF15)*256
230 FOR R=0 TO 29
240 FOR C=0 TO 39
250 A=B+R*S+C*2
260 POKE A,47+45*RND(2)
270 POKE A+1,110
280 NEXT
290 NEXT
300 GOTO 230
